    {
      "id": "claim_de69ba1d41f2416296efcb12a4dbc6d5",
      "statement": "OpenapiWebMvcConfigurer registers OpenapiAuthInterceptor on both the public and internal path patterns, and the interceptor decides per request which case applies (internal → pass, non-openapi → pass, public → verify). The operator-JWT filter also carves this surface out: OperatorJwtAuthenticationFilter short-circuits every path starting with /api/openapi because it uses sign auth instead.",
      "evidence": [
        {
