    {
      "id": "claim_3cf0fa2e111a4e728fe7aad3fcf81ab6",
      "statement": "timestamp accepts three parseable formats — 10-digit epoch seconds, ISO-8601 (with a space→T repair), or yyyy-MM-dd HH:mm:ss in the server zone. An unparseable timestamp throws IllegalArgumentException from parseTimestampSeconds, which is not an OpenapiAuthException, so it escapes the interceptor's catch block instead of producing the clean E4002 envelope — only a parseable but stale/future timestamp yields E4002.",
      "evidence": [
