    {
      "id": "claim_12200110575442c59f2231b94712c00a",
      "statement": "DeveloperInfoService materializes an openapi_developer row on first read: passport_uid comes from the company identity (or epochSeconds + companyId as fallback), eid from the company (or md5(passport_uid)), app_key = md5(passport_uid).substring(8, 24), and app_secret = md5(eid + common.openapi-rand-salt) — the salt (default \"ecshopx\") is fixed per environment and is only baked into newly generated secrets, so changing it never rewrites existing rows but silently desynchronizes environments that regenerate. The companys-bundle OpenapiDeveloperBootstrapService performs the same derivation for outbound credentials, with an app_key-collision fallback of md5(passport_uid + \"_\" + companyId).substring(8, 24) instead of failing.",
